  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The 49th ASEAN Summit, held in Manila, Philippines, served as a platform for regional leaders to discuss economic, security, and diplomatic priorities. Indonesian President Prabowo Subianto participated in several high-level meetings, including the ASEAN-Japan Summit and a special session involving the United States. A central focus of his address was the maintenance of peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific, where he cautioned major nations against escalating tensions. Furthermore, the Indonesian delegation emphasized regional cooperation on transnational crime and reaffirmed its stance on supporting Palestinian independence. On the economic front, Indonesia promoted its sustainable energy agenda, specifically targeting the expansion of solar power infrastructure and the implementation of B50 biodiesel standards. The event concluded with the formal handover of the ASEAN chairmanship to Singapore for 2027, following a series of diplomatic engagements involving leaders such as Donald Trump.",
